WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.176
Have you moved to Cyprus to work, to retire or with your family?

2
00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:07.427
The system may be quite different from what you know.

3
00:00:08.527 --> 00:00:12.009
Those entitled to GESY include people working in Cyprus,

4
00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:15.505
residents with permanent residence, their dependants,

5
00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:18.627
and EU citizens with a registered S1 form.

6
00:00:19.092 --> 00:00:21.286
If you are not entitled to GESY,

7
00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:23.910
you need private health insurance for everything.

8
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.249
For many residence permits, the Migration Department

9
00:00:28.249 --> 00:00:30.374
asks for private medical insurance even if

10
00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:33.902
you are in GESY, usually including repatriation.

11
00:00:34.461 --> 00:00:37.838
Check the current list of documents before you buy cover.

12
00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.748
If you buy a home with a loan,

13
00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:43.337
the bank will almost certainly ask for life cover.

14
00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:46.309
Ask whether it accepts your policy from home,

15
00:00:46.554 --> 00:00:50.512
and remember that cover for the loan leaves your family no income.

16
00:00:51.612 --> 00:00:55.024
While you work here, you pay social insurance contributions.

17
00:00:55.327 --> 00:00:58.392
Within the EU, periods of insurance in different countries count

18
00:00:58.392 --> 00:01:03.418
together towards your pension, but a state pension rarely covers the lifestyle you want,

19
00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:06.576
especially if you work here for only a few years.

20
00:01:07.676 --> 00:01:10.126
Read the full guide on avrastro.com,

21
00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:14.142
and book an appointment about your residence permit, mortgage or pension.
